    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_high_both">Resting HR is elevated and HRV is below your baseline, both classic signs of high activation. Prioritise rest, hydration and an easy day.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_high_else">Your autonomic markers are skewed toward stress today. Treat it as a recovery-focused day.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_high_hrv">HRV has dropped well below your baseline, pointing to elevated stress or fatigue. Ease off and give your body time to recover.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_high_rhr">Resting heart rate is running high versus your norm. Your body is under load today. Keep effort light.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_low_both">Resting heart rate is low and HRV is up. Your nervous system looks well-recovered and calm. A great day to push if you want to.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_low_else">Resting heart rate and HRV are sitting at or below baseline: low physiological stress. You\'re in a calm, recovered state.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_low_hrv">HRV is above baseline, a sign of a relaxed, well-recovered nervous system. Stress is low.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_medium_else">You\'re sitting around your typical autonomic baseline: moderate stress, a normal, balanced day.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_medium_hrv">Slightly off baseline (HRV is a little low), so you\'re moderately activated. Nothing alarming; just don\'t overreach.</string>
    <string name="i18n_g1_stress_tip_medium_rhr">Slightly off baseline (resting HR is a touch high), so you\'re moderately activated. Nothing alarming; just don\'t overreach.</string>
